  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;SHERBORNE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sherborne is a market town and civil parish in north west Dorset, in South West England. It is sited on the River Yeo, on the edge of the Blackmore Vale, east of Yeovil. The A30 road, which connects London to Penzance, runs through the town. In the 2011 census the population of Sherborne parish and the two electoral wards was 9,523. 28.7% of the population is aged 65 or older. Sherborne's historic buildings include Sherborne Abbey, its manor house, independent schools, and two castles: the ruins of a 12th-century fortified palace and the 16th-century mansion known as Sherborne Castle."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sherborne is a parish and electoral ward in Warwickshire, known for its historic buildings such as Sherborne Abbey and Sherborne Castle, and has a population of 1,234."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0110-a7a91f25c6d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YEOVIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yeovil is a town located east of Sherborne, mentioned in relation to the A30 road."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0110-a7a91f25c6d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LONDON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"London is mentioned as a destination connected to Penzance via the A30 road."</data>
